<h3>Bloodhorde Membership<o:p></o:p></h3>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>We accept :<o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:.5in;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
auto;margin-left:1.0in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]>1.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span><![endif]>any class from the Dark Elf, Troll, Ogre, or Iksar races <o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:.5in;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
auto;margin-left:1.0in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]>2.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span><![endif]>Shadow Knights and Necros from any race <o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:.5in;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
auto;margin-left:1.0in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]>3.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span><![endif]>Clerics of Cazic Thule or Bertoxxulus religions <o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:.5in;mso-margin-top-alt:auto;mso-margin-bottom-alt:
auto;margin-left:1.0in;text-indent:-.25in;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1;tab-stops:
list .5in'><![if !supportLists]>4.<span style='font:7.0pt "Times New Roman"'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
</span><![endif]>Characters must be of at least level 24 <o:p></o:p></p>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>If your character falls within
those basic guidelines, you must contact one of the guild recruiters concerning
your desired membership. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>If your character does not fall
within those guidelines, we will not accept you. Bloodhorde is a role-play
evil-only guild. Many of our members are in Bloodhorde for the main purpose
that they can role-play evil. If we were to allow non-evil characters within
the guild, we would severely disrupt the overall role-play environment for our
members. If you really want to be in Bloodhorde, you need a character that fits
those guidelines. We suggest starting a new character. Getting to lvl 24
doesn't take nearly as long as you think. Note that Bloodhorde will not offer
any &quot;power leveling&quot; services. An individual member may offer to
help, but the guild overall will <b>not</b> promise anything of that nature.<o:p></o:p></p>

<p style='margin-right:.5in;margin-left:.5in'>If you are granted membership,
you will be initiated as a minion of Bloodhorde. The minion rank is essentially
a trial period. This trial period will last for 21 days. After this time is up,
Horde Members are allowed to cast dissenting votes against the Minion if they
feel the Minion is not worthy of full membership and discuss the reasons with
officers. If a Minion receives one valid dissenting vote, they will be
disbanded from the guild. The 21 trial days can be shorter or longer based on
special individual cases. <o:p></o:p></p>

<p class=MsoNormal><![if !supportEmptyParas]>&nbsp;<![endif]><o:p></o:p></p>

